  "reasoning": "The patient presents with nausea, persistent chest pain, shivering, and anxiety. Nausea and chest pain are classic symptoms of gastrointestinal issues like peptic ulcer disease (PUD) or GERD. Shivering can be a physiological response to severe pain and stress, which aligns with the reported anxiety. Other conditions like hypertension, malaria, dengue, typhoid, pneumonia, asthma, and allergy do not fit the symptom profile as well because they typically present with fever, respiratory distress, or specific allergic signs that are absent here. The combination of nausea, chest/abdominal pain, and anxiety is most indicative of PUD.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]peptic ulcer disease[/DIAGNOSIS]"
